# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep host-installed
# dependencies out of the image.
#
# Why this file matters beyond context size:
# pnpm installs each workspace package's dependencies as symlinks into the
# top-level .pnpm store. If packages/<pkg>/node_modules is copied into the image
# *after* `pnpm install` has run there, it overwrites those symlinks and the
# dependencies become unresolvable. The visible symptom was:
#   Error: Cannot find module '/app/packages/database/node_modules/prisma/build/index.js'
# during `prisma generate`, even though the install step had created it correctly.
#
# Docker 29 does not apply the bare `node_modules` pattern to nested directories
# (verified: /node_modules was excluded, /packages/database/node_modules was not),
# so the pattern is written with an explicit leading `**/` to match at any depth.
**/node_modules

.git
.gitignore

# Build outputs
**/dist
**/.nuxt
**/.output
**/.turbo

# Judge runtime artifacts (scheduler and web app share this directory)
**/local_store
**/tmp

# Logs
**/*.log

# Test scratch dirs kept in the working tree
.test-problem

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# 本地部署密钥，禁止进入构建上下文（judge-machine Dockerfile 使用 COPY . /app）
**/.env
.env
